    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\nI extended the business-day rule in `BusinessDay.java` so the registration-date roll-forward now skips public holidays in addition to weekends:\n\n- Added the fixed holiday set (`2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`).\n- `rollForward` now advances a day whenever the date is a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed holiday, repeating until it lands on a non-holiday weekday. This correctly handles chained cases too (e.g. a date rolling onto `2026-12-25`/`2026-12-28` continues past both and any adjacent weekend).\n\nBecause `rollForward` is the single source of truth used by `BuildOwner`, `AssignMembershipNumber`, `CheckDailyOwnerLimit`, and `AssignBulkSignupWarning`, every derived value (stored date, membership-number year segment, daily-limit counting) now agrees on the holiday-aware business day.\n\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
