    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change extends the existing centralized `BusinessDay.rollForward` \u2014 the one place the Javadoc already names as the single definition every site agrees on. That is exactly the right unit for this rule.\n\n- The holiday list lives as a single `private static final Set<LocalDate> HOLIDAYS` constant, immutable via `Set.of`, right next to the logic that consumes it. No duplication, no new class or method needed.\n- The rule is folded into the existing roll-forward loop rather than bolted on as a separate pass, so weekend and holiday advancement share one coherent `plusDays(1)` walk \u2014 the natural way to express \"advance until a non-holiday weekday.\"\n- Javadoc on both the class and the method is updated to match, keeping the documented contract in sync.\n- No class or method is becoming a catch-all; the addition is purely additive and sits at the correct altitude.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this natural.",
